       _a_t_t_r.

       _s_t_a_c_k_a_d_d_r should point to the lowest addressable byte of  a  buffer  of
       _s_t_a_c_k_s_i_z_e bytes that was allocated by the caller.  The pages of the al‐
       located buffer should be both readable and writable.

       The  pptthhrreeaadd__aattttrr__ggeettssttaacckk()  function  returns  the  stack address and
       stack size attributes of the thread attributes object  referred  to  by
       _a_t_t_r  in  the  buffers  pointed  to by _s_t_a_c_k_a_d_d_r and _s_t_a_c_k_s_i_z_e, respec‐
       tively.

